# Shell scripts MUST keep LF line endings on every platform.
#
# Why: bash on Windows (Git for Windows / WSL / Cygwin) fails with
# "Input/output error" when shebang line is `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\n`
# instead of `#!/usr/bin/env bash\n`. The shebang gets parsed as
# `env bash\r` (with trailing CR) which doesn't exist as an executable.
# This bit Issue #16 — operator on Windows tried `bash scripts/deploy.sh`
# and got `/bin/bash: scripts/deploy.sh: Input/output error`.
#
# `text eol=lf` overrides any `core.autocrlf=true` global git config
# the operator might have on Windows. Files are stored LF in the repo
# AND checked out LF on every platform.
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
nginx/*.sh text eol=lf
nginx/nginx.conf.template text eol=lf

# Server-side configs read by Linux daemons — also LF-only.
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf

# Markdown: leave to the operator's preference (most editors handle
# both fine). No `eol` directive here — Git's default text handling
# applies (auto convert on Windows checkout if `core.autocrlf=true`).
